From: avb0795 project
Subject: [PATCH] ALTERED SOURCE: export temporary text from its active editor

Drag/slider widgets share an ID between text input and later pointer/keyboard
tweaks. The text undo state survives deactivation. Gate the deactivation export
on the active temporary editor so ending a later tweak preserves its value.

---
diff --git a/imgui_widgets.cpp b/imgui_widgets.cpp
--- a/imgui_widgets.cpp
+++ b/imgui_widgets.cpp
@@ -4605,6 +4605,10 @@ void ImGui::InputTextDeactivateHook(ImGuiID id)
         return;
     if (!state->EditedBefore)
         return;
+    // ALTERED SOURCE: a scalar can reuse this ID for a later non-text gesture.
+    // Export temporary text only while its editor owns the active interaction.
+    if ((state->Flags & ImGuiInputTextFlags_TempInput) && g.TempInputId != id)
+        return;
     //IMGUI_DEBUG_LOG_ACTIVEID("InputTextDeactivateHook() id = 0x%08X\n", id);
     g.InputTextDeactivatedState.ID = state->ID;
     g.InputTextDeactivatedState.ElapseFrame = g.FrameCount + 1;
